// Arbitrary-precision exact decimal (`perpuluhan`) — the numeric-tower Decimal slice.
//
// `perpuluhan("...")` parses a base-10 decimal of any precision into an exact
// value `mantissa * 10^-scale`, built on the proven `besar` bignum so it never
// overflows and never suffers binary-floating-point drift. Add/sub/mul are
// exact; division rounds half-to-even to 34 places then strips trailing zeros;
// comparison is value-based. The interpreter and the C backend evaluate it
// identically (byte-for-byte) — its arithmetic is what `DecimalModel.v` proves
// is a ring homomorphism to the rationals.
//
// (The WASM backend does not yet support Decimal; it fails closed rather than
// miscompiling — run this with the interpreter or the C backend.)

fungsi utama() -> Nombor kesan Tulis {
    biar a = perpuluhan("0.1");
    biar b = perpuluhan("0.2");

    cetakln(a + b);                                   // 0.3   (no float drift)
    cetakln(perpuluhan("19.99") * perpuluhan("3"));   // 59.97
    cetakln(perpuluhan("5") - perpuluhan("0.01"));    // 4.99
    cetakln(perpuluhan("1") / perpuluhan("4"));       // 0.25
    cetakln(perpuluhan("1") / perpuluhan("3"));       // 0.3333333333333333333333333333333333

    pulang 0;
}
